      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5acad9ecc9dba010c9c3ec68|full_name}: I found a fairly consistent testcase to demonstrate the non-pickup \"object sleeping\" issue...and also a really urgent one because it's going to degrade a lot of worlds with QvPen, at least when drawing certain letters.... since its widespread distribution at Vket 3, the QvPen has raced to become the most popular pen prefab in new worlds.\n\nSteps to reproduce:\n1. Go to my QVPen world from two clients, and make sure at least one is desktop: https://www.vrchat.com/home/launch?worldId=wrld_1483ac2f-bae4-464c-a33c-4c456bc48dd7\n2. Pick up a pen.\n3. For each V shape we draw, click and hold down the mouse: this is to ensure that there is sufficient time for the \"start drawing\" trigger to broadcast and rule out timing issues there.\n4. Quickly move the mouse in a V shape, but not so quickly that the IK gets lost. You should be able to see the pen move in the V shape on the other client.\n5. Wait at least a second before releasing the mouse for the same reason: waiting for object sync to interpolate and rule out ordering issues with the \"stop drawing\" trigger\n6. Repeat steps 3-5 as many times as needed for scientific accuracy.\n\nBefore getting to my observations let me make a quick note about how QvPen actually works: Each Pen has two object syncs:\n- The first object sync is a pickup (\"Grip\") - this does nothing except visually show the pen and provide ownership.\n- The second object sync is called \"SpawnTarget\": this one uses AutoCam to follow a transform located at the tip of the Grip, and has neither Rigidbody nor Pickup (this combination is what improves reliability in older vrchat versions)\n\nIn 2017, you will see the trail actually ahead of the physical pen \"Grip\", and overall well synced.\n\nIn 2018, things are somewhat reversed but also even worse. What I observe in 2018 is that the other client sees the pen move perfectly on time and in the V shape (if you don't see the pen move, you drew v too fast). However...the trail, if it syncs at all, is often over a second behind. Sometimes it is pretty close to the pen. Other times, it just won't go at all.\n\nNote that this bug does not affect some letters like \"o\" which is a favorite among Desktop users. I believe the shape of the \"v\" letter somehow improves the likelihood of invoking the object sleeping behavior which causes so much trouble.\n\nIn my attached screenshot, you can see the top client seeing very few lines drawn compared to the bottom client that drew them.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
